# Write a {{frameworkLabel}} test

1. Read `.testpilot/test-cases/normalized/<ID>.json` and `.testpilot/config.yaml`. Skip cases whose review verdict is MANUAL; ask before automating NEEDS-REWORK cases.
2. For each step, reuse a method or locator from `{{pagesDir}}`. If none exists, add it with the `create-page-object` skill. Locator order: {{locatorOrder}}.
3. Create or update the test in `{{testsDir}}/<area>/`{{#if isBdd}} (a feature file; its step definitions go next to the generated ones, above the `// testpilot:steps` marker){{/if}}:
{{#if isBdd}}
   ```gherkin
   @<ID> @<area> @<priority>
   Scenario: <ID> <title>
     Given <precondition, matched by one step definition>
     When <action>
     Then <expected result, an assertion in its step definition>
   ```
{{#if isSelenium}}
   ```java
   @When("<action text exactly as in the feature>")
   public void actionText() {
       LoginPage loginPage = context.page(LoginPage.class);
       loginPage.click(loginPage.signInButton);
   }

   @Then("<expected result text>")
   public void expectedResultText() {
       context.expect().heading("Products");
   }
   ```
   Step classes take a `TestContext` in their constructor (PicoContainer); `context.page(X.class)` returns the page object for the scenario. A scenario with TODO(testpilot) steps carries the `@testpilot-todo` tag (skipped by default); remove it once the steps are written.
{{else}}
   ```ts
   import { createBdd } from 'playwright-bdd';
   import { test } from '../src/fixtures/test';
   const { Given, When, Then } = createBdd(test);

   When('<action text exactly as in the feature>', async ({ loginPage }) => { await loginPage.signInButton.click(); });
   Then('<expected result text>', async ({ page }) => { await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Products' })).toBeVisible(); });
   ```
   Page objects come in as fixtures. A scenario with TODO(testpilot) steps carries the `@fixme` tag; remove it once the steps are written. Run `npx bddgen` before `npx playwright test`.
{{/if}}
{{else if isSelenium}}
   ```java
   public class <ID>Test extends BaseTest {
       @Test(description = "<ID> <title>", groups = {"<ID>", "<area>", "<priority>"})
       public void <titleInCamelCase>() {
           LoginPage loginPage = new LoginPage(driver);
           loginPage.loginAs("standard");
           expect.heading("Products");
       }
   }
   ```
   Page objects extend `BasePage` (`byRole`, `byLabel`, `byTestId`, `byText`, `type`, `click`, `select`); `expect` waits before it judges. A test with TODO(testpilot) steps calls `skipUntilDone("...")` first; delete that line once the steps are written.
{{else if isPlaywright}}
   ```{{ext}}
   {{#if isJs}}const { test, expect } = require('../../src/fixtures/test');{{else}}import { test, expect } from '../../src/fixtures/test';{{/if}}

   test('<ID> <title>', { tag: ['@<ID>', '@<priority>'], annotation: { type: 'test_key', description: '<ID>' } }, async ({ page }) => {
       await test.step('<step 1 action>', async () => { /* page object calls */ });
       await test.step('<step 1 expected>', async () => { await expect(/* locator */).toBeVisible(); });
   });
   ```
{{else if isAppium}}
   ```ts
   import { expect } from '@wdio/globals';

   import { loginScreen } from '../../../src/screens/LoginScreen';
   import { productsScreen } from '../../../src/screens/ProductsScreen';

   describe('<area>', () => {
       it('<ID> <title> @<ID> @<priority>', async () => {
           await loginScreen.loginAs('standard');
           await productsScreen.waitForScreen();
           await expect(productsScreen.cartButton).toBeDisplayed();
       });
   });
   ```
   Screen getters look elements up each time they are used; actions wait with `waitForDisplayed` (use `tap`, `type`, `choose` from `BaseScreen`). A test with TODO(testpilot) steps calls `pendingUntilDone(this, ...)` first; delete that line once the steps are written.
{{else}}
   Follow the existing tests' structure. Name the test `<ID> <title>` and tag it with the id so results trace back.
{{/if}}
4. Data comes from `test-data/` and secrets from environment variables via {{envHelper}}. Never hard-code either.
5. One behaviour per test. Every expected result becomes an assertion. No fixed sleeps.
6. Run only this test ({{runOneCommand}}) and make it pass twice in a row.
7. Update the case's row in `plans/automation-plan.md` (status: automated) or call TestPilot's `generate_tests`/`run_tests` tools, which do it for you.
